<section class="section-shell section-pad" id="architecture">
  <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">10 / System design</p><h2>Requests move through<br /><span class="muted-heading">clear responsibilities.</span></h2><p class="section-lede">An architecture concept: each layer transforms or routes the request before persistence.</p></div>
  <div class="architecture-panel"><div class="architecture-label"><span>REQUEST LIFECYCLE</span><span class="architecture-line"></span><span>01 — 06</span></div><div class="architecture-flow architecture-flow-wide"><div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon"><i class="bi bi-phone"></i></span><div><span class="arch-step">01 / INPUT</span><h3>Client</h3><p>Web · Mobile · Service</p></div><i class="bi bi-arrow-right arch-arrow"></i></div><div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon"><i class="bi bi-window"></i></span><div><span class="arch-step">02 / UI</span><h3>Frontend</h3><p>Present · Interact</p></div><i class="bi bi-arrow-right arch-arrow"></i></div><div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon"><i class="bi bi-signpost-split"></i></span><div><span class="arch-step">03 / ROUTING</span><h3>API Gateway</h3><p>Validate · Route</p></div><i class="bi bi-arrow-right arch-arrow"></i></div><div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon"><i class="bi bi-diagram-3"></i></span><div><span class="arch-step">04 / SERVICES</span><h3>Backend Services</h3><p>Compose · Coordinate</p></div><i class="bi bi-arrow-right arch-arrow"></i></div><div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon"><i class="bi bi-cpu"></i></span><div><span class="arch-step">05 / RULES</span><h3>Business Logic</h3><p>Rules · Events</p></div><i class="bi bi-arrow-right arch-arrow"></i></div><div class="arch-node arch-data"><span class="arch-icon"><i class="bi bi-hdd-stack"></i></span><div><span class="arch-step">06 / PERSISTENCE</span><h3>Database / Redis / Queue</h3><p>Store · Cache · Decouple</p></div></div></div><div class="architecture-foot"><i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i> Conceptual diagram for learning and discussion, not a claim about a deployed production system.</div></div>
